==Aftermath and reactions==
===Domestic reactions===
Morrison conceded defeat and resigned as leader of the [[Liberal Party of Australia|Liberal Party]]; his successor will be decided at the next Liberal party room meeting.<ref name=resign>{{cite web|last1=Hitch|first1=Georgia|url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-21/federal-election-live-blog-scott-morrison-anthony-albanese/101085640|title=Morrison says he will resign as leader of Liberal Party|publisher=ABC|date=21 April 2022|access-date=21 April 2022|archive-date=21 April 2022}}</ref> Albanese claimed victory and acknowledged Morrison's concession. He thanked his supporters, his colleagues, and his team for the win. He pledged to fulfill the promise of the [[Uluru Statement from the Heart]], not to leave anyone behind, and to unite Australia for a better future. He promised to end the climate wars and to commit to the pledges he has made during the election campaign.<ref>{{cite web |date=2022-05-21 |title=Australian election 2022: Anthony Albanese claims victory for Labor as Scott Morrison stands down as Liberal leader – live updates |url=https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2022/may/21/australian-election-2022-live-news-today-australia-federal-anthony-albanese-scott-morrison-who-won-winning-opinion-polls-polling-vote-labor-coalition-liberals-greens-independents-candidates-seats-odds-results-politics-latest-updates |access-date=2022-05-21 |website=the Guardian}}</ref> [[Australian Greens]] leader [[Adam Bandt]] celebrated his party's historic two seat gains in [[Queensland]], one each from the [[Liberal National Party of Queensland|Liberals]] and [[Australian Labor Party|Labor]], with a prospect of gaining another seat from the Liberals. He called this a historic "greenslide" as he thanked a record number of people in Queensland who voted Greens for the first time in this election.<ref>{{cite news |date=2022-05-22 |title='A microcosm of progressivism': Queensland Greens celebrate historic 'greenslide' in Brisbane as rivals go to ground |work=ABC News |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-22/qld-federal-election-lnp-regroup-as-greens-celebrate-major-win/101083852 |access-date=2022-05-22}}</ref>

Two days after the election, Governor-General [[David Hurley]] swore in Albanese, deputy leader [[Richard Marles]], [[Jim Chalmers]], and Senators [[Penny Wong]] and [[Katy Gallagher]] as an interim five-person government. Although counting was still underway, the swearing in was expedited due to an upcoming meeting of the [[Quadrilateral Security Dialogue]]. The five ministers will divide all portfolios between them until the full ministry is sworn in. According to [[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]], Hurley would not have sworn in Albanese without assurances that Labor could provide stable government, as well as legal advice that this was the proper course of action.<ref name="swornin-abc">{{cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-23/anthony-albanese-sworn-in-australian-prime-minister/101089902 |title=Anthony Albanese and four senior frontbenchers sworn in ahead of Quad trip |last=Worthington |first=Brett |date=23 May 2022 |work=ABC News |access-date=23 May 2022}}</ref> At his first press conference after being sworn in, Albanese announced that he received assurances that crossbenchers [[Rebekha Sharkie]], [[Bob Katter]], [[Andrew Wilkie]], [[Helen Haines]], and [[Zali Steggall]] would provide supply and would not support a [[no-confidence motion]] against the government.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.skynews.com.au/australia-news/politics/prime-minister-anthony-albanese-confirms-deal-with-existing-crossbenchers-to-secure-confidence-amid-election-victory/news-story/0c515548eaa95a1278ba4878aabbf6c5 |title=Prime Minister Anthony Albanese confirms deal with existing crossbenchers to secure confidence amid election victory |last=Clarke|first=Tyrone|date=23 May 2022 |publisher=Sky News Australia|access-date=25 May 2022}}</ref>

===International reactions===
{{Update section|date=May 2022}}
Several world leaders issued statements congratulating Albanese on his victory.
* {{flag|Canada}}: Prime Minister [[Justin Trudeau]] released an official statement congratulating Albanese on his victory.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2022/05/21/statement-prime-minister-results-general-election-australia|title=Statement by the Prime Minister on the results of the general election in Australia|work=Canada.ca|date=21 May 2022|accessdate=22 May 2022}}</ref>
* {{flag|China}}: Premier [[Li Keqiang]] sent a message congratulating Albanese on his election win, ending two years of diplomatic freeze on a ministerial level between the two countries. He stated that China is ready to work with the new government and it is in the interests of both countries to have "sound and stable relations".<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/chinese-premier-congratulates-anthony-albanese-on-victory-hopes-for-sound-and-stable-relations-20220524-p5anzj.html|title=Chinese premier congratulates Anthony Albanese on victory, hopes for 'sound and stable' relations|newspaper=The Sydney Morning Herald |date=24 May 2022|access-date=24 May 2022|author=Galloway, Anthony}}</ref>
* {{flag|Fiji}}: Prime Minister [[Frank Bainimarama]] congratulated Albanese and "welcomed" his plan for the Pacific "to put climate first".<ref>{{cite web |last=Singh |first=Shanil|title=Bainimarama sends well wishes to new Australian PM |url=https://www.fijivillage.com/news/Bainimarama-sends-well-wishes-to-new-Australian-PM-8fxr54/ |access-date=2022-05-23 |website=Fiji Village|date=May 22, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Manager |first=Ritika Pratap Deputy News |title=Albanese ready to work with Pacific countries |url=https://www.fbcnews.com.fj/news/albanese-ready-to-work-with-pacific-countries/ |access-date=2022-05-23 |website=Fiji Broadcasting Corporation}}</ref>
* {{flag|France}}: At a May 21 press conference, the then-outgoing foreign affairs minister [[Jean-Yves Le Drian]] said: "I can't stop myself from saying that the defeat of Morrison suits me very well." He was referencing Australia's cancellation of [[Attack-class submarine|a French–Australian submarine deal]] under the Morrison government.<ref>{{cite news |last=Torsoli |first=Albertina |date=2022-05-21 |title=France's Le Drian Says He's Happy Scott Morrison Lost Election |work=[[Bloomberg.com]] |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-05-21/france-s-le-drian-says-he-s-happy-australia-prime-minister-lost |access-date=2022-05-22}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=2022-05-21 |title=France's outgoing foreign minister welcomes defeat of Scott Morrison |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/21/frances-outgoing-foreign-minister-welcomes-defeat-of-scott-morrison |access-date=2022-05-25 |website=the Guardian |language=en|author=Badshah, Nadeem}}</ref> President [[Emmanuel Macron]] also hinted at the deal when he called Albanese on 26 May, both vowing to "rebuild a bilateral relationship founded on trust and respect".<ref>{{Cite news |date=27 May 2022 |title=Emmanuel Macron agrees to 'rebuild' France-Australia ties during phone call with Anthony Albanese |work=[[ABC News (Australia)]] |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-27/emmanuel-macron-agrees-to-rebuild-france-australia-ties-albanese/101107132 |access-date=28 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220527102420/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-27/emmanuel-macron-agrees-to-rebuild-france-australia-ties-albanese/101107132 |archive-date=27 May 2022}}</ref>
* {{flag|India}}: Prime Minister [[Narendra Modi]] sent his congratulations to Albanese, highlighting his commitment to the [[Australia–India Comprehensive Strategic Partnership]].<ref name="india-response">{{cite web |title=PM Modi congratulates new Australian counterpart Anthony Albanese |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/current-affairs/pm-modi-congratulates-new-australian-counterpart-anthony-albanese-122052100917_1.html |website=Business Standard India |access-date=21 May 2022 |date=21 May 2022}}</ref>
* {{flag|New Zealand}}: Prime Minister [[Jacinda Ardern]] congratulated Albanese, stating that she was looking forward "to working with him on a range of issues including supporting New Zealanders living in Australia, making trans-Tasman business even easier, deepening our partnership with our close friends in the Pacific, and advancing our interests on the world stage."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/467618/jacinda-ardern-congratulates-incoming-australian-prime-minister-anthony-albanese|title=Jacinda Ardern congratulates incoming Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese|work=RNZ|date=22 May 2022|accessdate=22 May 2022}}</ref> 
* {{flag|Singapore}}: Prime Minister [[Lee Hsien Loong]] sent a letter to Albanese congratulating his election win, citing their shared longstanding ties and expressed his desire to work with him to continue advancing [[Australia–Singapore relations]].<ref>{{cite news |author1=Tiffany Ang |title=PM Lee congratulates Australia's Prime Minister-elect Anthony Albanese on election win |url=https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/pm-lee-hsien-loong-congratulates-australia-antony-albanese-2699201 |access-date=22 May 2022 |work=[[CNA (TV network)|CNA]] |publisher=[[Mediacorp]] |date=22 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220522153357/https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/pm-lee-hsien-loong-congratulates-australia-antony-albanese-2699201 |archive-date=22 May 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Auto |first1=Hermes |title=PM Lee sends letter of congratulations to Australian PM-elect Anthony Albanese |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/asia/se-asia/pm-lee-sends-letter-of-congratulations-to-australian-pm-elect-anthony-albanese |access-date=22 May 2022 |work=[[The Straits Times]] |publisher=[[SPH Media Trust]] |date=22 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220522153843/https://www.straitstimes.com/asia/se-asia/pm-lee-sends-letter-of-congratulations-to-australian-pm-elect-anthony-albanese |archive-date=22 May 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>
* {{flag|United Kingdom}}: Prime Minister [[Boris Johnson]] congratulated Albanese on [[Twitter]], saying that he looks forward to working with him on strengthening [[Australia–United Kingdom relations]] on trade and [[AUKUS]] partnership.<ref name="uk-reaction">{{cite web |title=Live: Albanese promises to bring Australians together, fully commits to Uluru Statement from the Heart |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-05-21/federal-election-live-blog-scott-morrison-anthony-albanese/101085640#live-blog-post-1211502315 |website=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |access-date=21 May 2022 |date=20 May 2022}}</ref> The leader of the UK [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] and [[Leader of the Opposition (United Kingdom)|opposition leader]], [[Keir Starmer]], congratulated Albanese for ending "almost a decade of stale conservative rule".<ref>{{cite tweet|number=1528012688453935105 |title= A positive campaign by @AustralianLabor ends almost a decade of stale Conservative rule. You showed that Australia deserves better. Huge congratulations to @AlboMP and our sister party Australian Labor! | date= 2022-05-21 |access-date=2022-05-21 |website=Twitter |user=keir_starmer |first=Keir |last=Starmer |author-link=Keir Starmer}}</ref> 
* {{flag|United States}}: President [[Joe Biden]] called Albanese on 22 May, congratulating him and reaffirming the US' commitment towards their bilateral relationship with Australia. Ahead of the Quad summit taking place two days later, Biden appreciated Albanese's commitment towards the security alliance and his decision to participate in the summit.<ref>{{Cite news |date=22 May 2022 |title=Joe Biden calls Anthony Albanese to congratulate him on election victory |website=[[Special Broadcasting Service|SBS News]] |publisher=[[Agence France-Presse]]/[[Australian Associated Press]] |url=https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/joe-biden-calls-anthony-albanese-to-congratulate-him-on-election-victory/epovurjs8 |url-status=live |access-date=22 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220522132958/https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/joe-biden-calls-anthony-albanese-to-congratulate-him-on-election-victory/epovurjs8 |archive-date=22 May 2022}}</ref>

Albanese also received messages of congratulations from the leaders of [[Bangladesh]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.thedailystar.net/news/bangladesh/diplomacy/news/sheikh-hasina-greets-australian-labor-leader-anthony-albanese-election-victory-3029051 |title=Sheikh Hasina greets Australian Labor leader Anthony Albanese on election victory |date=May 22, 2022 |newspaper=[[The Daily Star (Bangladesh)|The Daily Star]] |place=Dhaka}}}</ref> [[Indonesia]],<ref>{{cite tweet |user=jokowi |number=1528569773188976641 |date=May 23, 2022 |title=Congratulations Anthony Albanese @AlboMP  on your election as Prime Minister of Australia! Look forward to working closely with you in advancing our Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, including the concrete implementation of IA-CEPA |first=Joko |last=Widodo |author-link=Joko Widodo}}</ref> [[Israel]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/bennett-congratulates-new-australian-prime-minister/|title=Bennett congratulates new Australian prime minister|website=www.timesofisrael.com}}</ref> [[Italy]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.afr.com/politics/federal/from-biden-to-bin-night-albanese-s-big-week-out-20220526-p5aon4|title=From Biden to bin night: Albanese's big week out|date=26 May 2022|website=Australian Financial Review}}</ref> [[Japan]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/05/24/remarks-by-president-biden-prime-minister-kishida-fumio-of-japan-prime-minister-narendra-modi-of-india-and-prime-minister-anthony-albanese-of-australia-at-the-second-in-person-quad-leaders/|title=Remarks by President Biden, Prime Minister Kishida Fumio of Japan, Prime Minister Narendra Modi of India, and Prime Minister Anthony Albanese of Australia at the Second In-Person Quad Leaders' Summit|date=24 May 2022|website=The White House}}</ref> the [[Netherlands]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/world/2022/05/australian-election-labor-s-anthony-albanese-wins-scott-morrison-quits-as-liberal-party-leader.html|title=Australian election: Labor's Anthony Albanese wins, Scott Morrison quits as Liberal party leader|via=www.newshub.co.nz}}</ref> [[Pakistan]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.radio.gov.pk/22-05-2022/pm-shehbaz-felicitates-anthony-albanese-on-his-election-as-next-prime-minister-of-australia|title=PM felicitates Albanese on his election as Australian PM|website=www.radio.gov.pk}}</ref> [[Papua New Guinea]],<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.looppng.com/node/112624|title=PM Congratulates Albanese, Thanks Morrison |date=24 May 2022|website=Loop PNG}}</ref> [[Samoa]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.samoaobserver.ws/category/samoa/98409|title=Fiame welcomes new Australian Prime Minister|website=Samoa Observer}}</ref> [[Saudi Arabia]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://arab.news/8eguk|title=Saudi leaders congratulate new Australian PM on being sworn in|date=24 May 2022|website=Arab News}}</ref> the [[Solomon Islands]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.solomontimes.com/news/sogavare-congratulates-albanese-on-his-election-win/11869|title=Sogavare Congratulates Albanese on His Election Win – Solomon Times Online|website=SolomonTimes.com|date=May 24, 2022}}</ref> [[Sri Lanka]],<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.adaderana.lk/news/82594/president-rajapaksa-congratulates-australian-prime-minister-elect |title=President Rajapaksa congratulates Australian prime minister-elect |date=May 22, 2022 |work=Ada Derana}}</ref> and [[Vietnam]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://nhandan.vn/tin-tuc-su-kien/thu-chuc-mung-ong-anthony-albanese-duoc-bau-lam-thu-tuong-australia-698848/ |title=Thư chúc mừng ông Anthony Albanese được bầu làm Thủ tướng Australia |lang=Vietnamese |trans-title=Letter of congratulation to Mr. Anthony Albanese on being elected Prime Minister of Australia |date=26 May 2022 |website=Báo Nhân Dân}}</ref>

